      "writtenOn": "2024-10-22T01:16:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Gwendal,\n\n`task_set_event(TASK_ID_MOTIONSENSE, CONFIG_ACCEL_LIS2DW12_INT_EVENT);` should just wake up the `motion_sense_task` but I don\u0027t find where uses the `evevt(CONFIG_ACCEL_LIS2DW12_INT_EVENT or CONFIG_ACCEL_BMA4XX_INT_EVENT)`, so there should no limitation for 2 identical sensors are configured with interrupt mode?\n\nI alse found the `karis` and `kanix` configured 2 identical sensors with interrupt mode.\n\nI also tested the CL with **base sensor: lis2dw12 + lid sensor: lis2dw12** and **base sensor: bma422 + lid sensor: bma422**, both of them PASSED 1000 cycles `AccelerometersGroup`, but they can not pass 100 cycles without this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "95a089cb_b1dde3cf",
      "revId": "38a12ae726a702dc9d3e30aa67e882d6434c775f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e7c5953_f620e9f6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-24T04:32:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is happening is the lid_ and base_ interrupt both set the same bit inside TASK_EVENT_MOTION_INTERRUPT_MASK. So when the bit is set, both sensors (lid and base) irq_handler is called. It means that the irq_handler() function is called 2x more than expected, since it is unlikely the sensors are perfectly in sync. \nSo it works in the sense the test pass, but this is not the intent of the code.\n\nIt would be interesting to see why the GPIO based approach (forced mode) is not working.",
      "parentUuid": "eb3b5a6b_8e43a13e",
      "revId": "38a12ae726a702dc9d3e30aa67e882d6434c775f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
